  "details": "The audio spatial positioning bug is still quite prevalent in VRChat, however I believe have actually identified the cause; \nOnce it starts affecting your game, the log file fills with multiple examples of these two errors;\nLog        -  [Behaviour] uSpeak [13][1648381228]: Segment playback time didn't match audio data length, audio cpu usage may be too high! - playbackTimeMS/audioLengthMS: 9061/8800\nAnd\nLog        -  [Behaviour] uSpeak [1][1648388069] (every 10): voice buffer underrun, sample arrived 12ms late.\nLooks like something in uSpeak is crashing or suffering a memory leak and it just can't keep up with player positions so it sounds like it's coming from your ear rather than the other player's heads.",
